oats make `19.99 * 100` come out as `1998.9999\u2026`, so it became 1998 cents. The same truncation turned 0.29 into 28 and 4.35 into 434.\n\n**Fix:** It now converts through `Decimal(str(amount))` and rounds half up to the nearest cent.\n\nI introduced an indentation error partway through the edit and fixed it before the final run. The final diff is only the `to_cents` change plus the `Decimal` import.\n\n`to_cents` rounds half up, so a price with more than two decimal places (for example 0.005) rounds to the nearest cent instead of truncating. Nothing in the repo does this today.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 8, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 151488, "requests_cache_write": 21675, "requests_cost_usd": 0.0888523, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 18, "requests_output": 1948, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial6", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 11, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T23:13:42.504924+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 20.335, "t_checker_s": 0.325, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1966, "tokens_cache_read": 151488, "tokens_cache_write": 21675, "tokens_fresh": 1966, "tokens_input_uncached": 18, "tokens_main_cache_read": 151488, "tokens_main_cache_write": 21675, "tokens_main_calls": 8, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 18, "tokens_main_output": 1948, "tokens_output": 1948, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 151488, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 21675, "token